  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>CH</mi></math> is converted to ketone by catalytic hydration with reagents.</p><p>Hydration of alkynes is carried out in the presence of a warm 40% sulfuric acid in the presence of 1% mercuric sulfate.</p><p>In this reaction, first a molecule of water is added to form enol which then tautomerizes to keto form.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/e34665d5-bd51-4277-93ad-ac699119b381-image.png\" style=\"width: 524px; height: 100px;\" /></p>",
